cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: DeterministicSequentialEmission.jl
abstract: >-
  The deterministic sequential emission treatment of prompt neutron emission from fission
  fragments: the energy conservation equation of every emission sequence is solved separately,
  with Weisskopf-Ewing evaporation spectra in the centre-of-mass system and fragment level
  densities in the Fermi-gas regime. Because the number of sequences is an integer at every
  fragment configuration, the post-neutron fragment mass is an integer without rounding.
  Multiplicities, residual quantities and the laboratory prompt neutron spectrum are contracted
  against measured fragment yields.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gogîță
    given-names: Paul-Adrian
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/PaulGoG/DeterministicSequentialEmission.jl
keywords:
